{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-universal-homeomorphisms}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f15ba0d1d1b51975ac72cdf431fbce887f3489d597f434517da1924220db0290", "source_text": "Universal homeomorphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6bb44577a8a706f8788443e83ab27ffdb93c047f67b5b64a9567864a5d2c4463", "unit_id": "tag:04DC:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-universal-homeomorphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:29153c3587f2e6983bd08174dc5e1fc5813a17d3bbb7351e7db78233570315f3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following definition is really superfluous since a universal\nhomeomorphism is really just an integral, universally injective\nand surjective morphism, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6a6bd71c474521273d6655f3130539a1e4bbbe929ef220ba2f254c5e96b295fb", "unit_id": "tag:04DC:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f' : Y' \\times_Y X \\to Y'$", "MATH_0003": "$Y' \\to Y$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-universal-homeomorphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:15e896c833400bb71bd5e10b1deaee1e99cdcd2236196c80da244c3bd092b2b5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d6d2f367fba21f9942401d81cf5aae6f602a2872482a5e0e76d2d563a455f56b", "source_text": "A morphism <MATH_0001> of schemes is called a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>universal homeomorphism<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif the base change <MATH_0002> is a homeomorphism for\nevery morphism <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aca7727cc91d9054e9abbcbd97475a34f7d859da55becb132bc35083fc62a9f5", "unit_id": "tag:04DD:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6a3a1c9a82de247bafeb87228ee209ee79f194a3e677946381032da5f1885528", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFirst we state the obligatory lemmas.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3293165f177a1c1d485dbc733942e1d175d6e11731df32a66cf8fdd036b7642d", "unit_id": "tag:04DC:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-universal-homeomorphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:57b3e4c2871c0d8a728894922412df0cd3b87db46a580a391fbedfa4f6583667", "source_text": "The base change of a universal homeomorphism of schemes\nby any morphism of schemes is a universal homeomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dbaa9ec3cbda910daa5d1efbdc59306096ded3ef0d70060814e53fbf5bced32c", "unit_id": "tag:0CEU:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1aea928c2054a1d8aedbb40f94195161b290fc35e1d26892238429f8986f54d5", "source_text": "This is immediate from the definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ed527da30f69c9bcc90112222bdf3d207c927d6febb801818b673598175ce475", "unit_id": "tag:0CEU:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-composition-universal-homeomorphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:99e724ba0e39f8eb32db0e4e3a1e37c54e2c4ccdf8816213fc6173849b6cae15", "source_text": "The composition of a pair of universal homeomorphisms of\nschemes is a universal homeomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f65a7d5ca040e032ef87fa032032bfc4cb3da05b1e93c3541026625d2afdd96", "unit_id": "tag:0CEV:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1aea928c2054a1d8aedbb40f94195161b290fc35e1d26892238429f8986f54d5", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:0CEV:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6a3a1c9a82de247bafeb87228ee209ee79f194a3e677946381032da5f1885528", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following simple lemma is the key to characterizing universal\nhomeomorphisms.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7aae28ac303005d0081adb8787e47ef356ddbad89a22b97dda3bb30f396a7f2a", "unit_id": "tag:04DC:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-homeomorphism-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7a84a003918335aa24b87cb22dad573df64c9867df00214403103f6ad720d279", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:de8d66601241bbfa72049ebc600485508cd49f53ee356054c054b9145a87e107", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. If <MATH_0002> is a homeomorphism\nonto a closed subset of <MATH_0003> then <MATH_0004> is affine.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cc89f75a3b59649322486eb72e557758118ac370bd63f0636753af9bb6fa723e", "unit_id": "tag:04DE:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$y \\in Y$", "MATH_0002": "$y \\not \\in f(X)$", "MATH_0003": "$y$", "MATH_0004": "$f(X)$", "MATH_0005": "$y \\in f(X)$", "MATH_0006": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$y$", "MATH_0009": "$y \\in V$", "MATH_0010": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0011": "$x$", "MATH_0012": "$V$", "MATH_0013": "$f(U) \\subset V \\cap f(X)$", "MATH_0014": "$f$", "MATH_0015": "$h \\in \\Gamma(V, \\mathcal{O}_Y)$", "MATH_0016": "$y \\in D(h)$", "MATH_0017": "$D(h) \\cap f(X) \\subset f(U)$", "MATH_0018": "$h' \\in \\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0019": "$f^\\sharp(h)$", "MATH_0020": "$U$", "MATH_0021": "$D(h') \\subset U$", "MATH_0022": "$f^{-1}(D(h))$", "MATH_0023": "$Y$", "MATH_0024": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6a4ae83dc16176a2fa42e0c2d0075f3561397fde1cbd81c641a16be0370f1ee0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:929a039a4e2eb8887943c5edf677ff2ac50bddf833844abe2bbffcc27b31c2b2", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a point. If <MATH_0002>, then there exists\nan affine neighbourhood of <MATH_0003> which is disjoint from <MATH_0004>.\nIf <MATH_0005>, let <MATH_0006> be the unique point of <MATH_0007> mapping to <MATH_0008>.\nLet <MATH_0009> be an affine open neighbourhood.\nLet <MATH_0010> be an affine open neighbourhood of <MATH_0011> which maps into <MATH_0012>.\nSince <MATH_0013> is open in the induced topology by our\nassumption on <MATH_0014> we may choose a\n<MATH_0015> such that <MATH_0016>\nand <MATH_0017>. Denote <MATH_0018>\nthe restriction of <MATH_0019> to <MATH_0020>. Then we see that\n<MATH_0021> is equal to <MATH_0022>. In other words, every point\nof <MATH_0023> has an open neighbourhood whose inverse image is affine.\nThus <MATH_0024> is affine, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d1b616aa025da9c9c6f7b70d6ed195780d5aec41411546ec55caeb4f4213014", "unit_id": "tag:04DE:proof"}
